==Battleground==
*1 [[Primeval Cyclone]] spawns as the boss after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*6 [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>, delay 3~5 seconds<sup>90f~150f</sup>.
*1 [[Sir Rel]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Li'l Bun Bun]]s spawn after 76.67 seconds<sup>2,300f</sup>, delay 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 93.33 seconds<sup>2,800f</sup>, delay 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Using a [[Talents|Talented]] [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Rodeo Cat]] and [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]], it is possible to stall the Primeval Cyclone almost as effectively as using [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] against some of the other Cyclones.

[[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Prof. Cat Jobs]], along with a Weaken UP (M) [[Cat Combo|Combo]] (e.g. [[Power of Darkness (Combo)|Power of Darkness]]) can almost completely nullify the boss. Simply send out some tough meatshields with the Professor in the back and weaken it. Then finish it off with some damage dealers (e.g. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]). [[:Category:Cats with Slow ability|Cats with Slow]]/[[:Category:Cats with Freeze ability|Freeze]] abilities are recommended to bring along too.

Note that in close range, the Primeval Cyclone can easily destroy most of your cats, especially with its enormous strength boost of 200% at half health, so it is important to keep this enemy at range with any kind of stalling possible. Do note that if the player happens to own [[Trixi the Merc (Uber Rare Cat)|Trixi the Revenant]], then this level will be incredibly easy if she is given time to deal with the cyclone while it is alone.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Rodeo Cat]] - Almost required in this stage, as he is able to slow both Gory Dark and the Primeval Cyclone at the same time.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Fortune Teller Cat (Rare Cat)|Doctor Cat]] - Can be a helpful unit, but be wary of his high knockback chance, as more than 1 or 2 can  knockback the cyclone behind the enemy base, causing your attackers to die.
*[[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]] - Crucial for victory, as their weaken can keep the cyclone at bay and let your meatshields live longer, as well as give your close range attacker to get a hit in on the peons without dying.
*[[Delinquent Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ultra Delinquent Cat]] - This unit can provide an important boost to your damage and overall control over this stage, as he allows you to use close ranged attackers (e.g. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]) and deal more damage than you would be able to without this freeze effect.
*[[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Prof. Cat Jobs]] - Can be used to almost completely nullify the cyclone, allowing you to easily kill it if you lure it to your base. (This may take a few tries, but [[Cat Cannon|Slow Cat Cannon]] can assist in this)
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] - Deals massive damage to Dark Enemies and can deal significant damage to the Gory Darks, preventing them from pushing through your meatshields and killing your stack of crowd controllers.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] - Similarly to Pizza Cat, Can Can Cat can deal high amounts of damage, but to a single target.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Trixi the Merc (Uber Rare Cat)|Trixi the Revenant]] - Similarly to Delinquent Cat, Trixi provide a significant freeze effect. Although this effect is shorter, she has a fast attack rate with a high freeze chance to make up for this.
*Most [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]] units work well here, as their abilites against traited enemies are very useful.
*[[Gaia the Creator (Legend Rare Cat)|Gaia the Supreme]] - Deals insane damage against traited enemies with Multi-Hit at the cost of a blindspot of 200, meaning you have to protect her well in order for her to not die.

